Hybrid

DEPT® is a Growth Invention company built to help the world’s most ambitious brands grow faster. Operating at the intersection of technology and marketing, our 4,000+ specialists deliver growth invention services across Brand & Media, Experience, Commerce, CRM, and Technology & Data. We’re 50|50 tech and marketing, partner-led, and first to move. Clients include Google, Lufthansa, Meta, eBay, and OpenAI. We have been certified B Corp and Climate Neutral since 2021.

JOB PURPOSE

This role is part of our Experience & Engineering team based in the Netherlands. We combine our skills in developing future-ready technical solutions with our expertise in creating beautiful designs to deliver exceptional and engaging digital experiences that build lasting relationships with our clients like Gant, Inter Milan, bol.com and Just Eat Takeaway.

As an Android Developer, you will play a key role in designing, developing, and maintaining high-quality mobile applications that deliver exceptional user experiences. Collaborating closely with our international team, you will translate complex design specifications into functional, innovative features while continuously seeking ways to improve the app and stay ahead of industry trends. Your proactive approach and technical expertise will ensure the delivery of reliable, user-centric solutions that meet client needs and drive business success.

KEY RESPONSIBILITIES

Collaborate closely with cross-functional teams to design, develop, and deliver high-quality mobile applications;

Translate complex design specifications and client requirements into functional, user-friendly Android features;

Continuously improve app performance, usability, and reliability to enhance the overall user experience;

Stay ahead of industry trends and emerging technologies to propose innovative solutions and improvements;

Ensure code quality by adhering to best practices, including SOLID principles and design patterns like MVVM;

Participate in the full mobile development lifecycle, from concept and design to testing and deployment;

Take ownership of the end product, proactively identifying and resolving issues to maintain app stability;

Communicate effectively with team members and stakeholders to align development efforts with business goals;

Mentor and support junior developers, fostering a collaborative and knowledge-sharing environment.

WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR

3 - 5 years of professional experience in Android development;

Strong proficiency in Kotlin and Jetpack Compose;

Experience with Kotlin Multiplatform is a plus;

Solid understanding of Android frameworks and the full mobile development lifecycle;

Familiarity with SOLID programming principles and design patterns such as MVVM;

Previous experience with Java is a plus;

Proven problem-solving skills and ability to work independently;

Excellent communication skills in English, both written and spoken;

Ability to collaborate effectively with cross-disciplinary teams;

Proactive mindset with a strong sense of responsibility for the end product;

Eagerness to learn and stay updated with the latest mobile and UX technologies.

WE OFFER

A flexible, hybrid working policy (2-3 days from the office, depending on location) and the opportunity to work from abroad for 13 weeks a year.

24 vacation days per year and the possibility to buy an unlimited number of extra vacation days.

DEPT®/YOU Learning Menu and DEPT®/YOU Special Programs. Develop your skills with courses and programs tailored to your needs.

Stay happy and healthy with a contribution to your health through the OpenUp platform, gym and wellness discounts, and healthy lunches at the office.

A reputation for doing good. DEPT® has been a Certified B Corp® since 2021 and named ‘Agency of the Year’ at both The Lovies and The Webby Awards.

Awesome clients. Whether big or small, local or global — at DEPT® you’ll get the opportunity to work with clients of all sizes and across all industries. And we celebrate all of our successes together!

The opportunity for possibility. We want to enable you to do what you do best and help you develop your skills further with training, development and certifications.

Global annual DEPT® Cares Month in which employees come together and donate their skills to support local charities.

WHY DEPT®?

We are a Growth Invention company built to help the world’s most ambitious brands grow faster. Operating at the intersection of technology and marketing, we create what is next by pioneering ideas, acting fast, and moving further because standing still just is not in our DNA.

We are drawn to people who stay curious, move with intent, and never stop inventing. Our culture runs on three values: better together, relentlessly curious, and get sh*t done. It is how we work, how we grow, and how we make things that matter.

At DEPT®, you will find the freedom to explore, the space to collaborate, and the trust to make a real impact for our clients, for each other, and for the world we are helping to build.

DIVERSITY, EQUITY & INCLUSION

At DEPT®, we take pride in creating an inclusive workplace where everyone has an equal opportunity to thrive. We actively seek to recruit, develop, nurture, and retain talented individuals from diverse backgrounds, with varying skills and perspectives.

Not sure you meet all qualifications? Apply, and let us decide! Research shows that women and members of underrepresented groups tend not to apply for jobs when they think they may not meet every requirement, when in fact they do. We believe in giving everyone a fair chance to shine.

We also encourage you to reach out to us and discuss any reasonable adjustments we can make to support you throughout the recruitment process and your time with us.

Want to know more about our dedication to diversity, equity, and inclusion? Check out our efforts here.

Wat ga je doen?
Goede kwaliteit van data is niet alleen nodig om de politietaak uit te voeren, het is ook een voorwaarde om aan de wet te voldoen en RAPP te laten functioneren. De rol van data steward is nieuw in ons programma. Het is aan jou om dit samen met de andere collega’s vorm te gaan geven. Je taken bestaan onder andere uit:
Toezicht houden op de datakwaliteit van RAPP met betrekking tot:Naleving van wet- en regelgeving (Wet politiegegevens);
Technische Datakwaliteit;
De eenduidigheid en standaarden van referentie- en stamgegevens.

Gebruiken van dashboards en ad hoc query’s om toezicht te kunnen houden;
Verbeteren van datakwaliteitseisen;
Aandragen van verbeteringen van de applicatie in het Programma Vernieuwend Registreren;
Corrigeren van technische data over vele registraties heen;
Samenwerken met Functioneel Beheer bij het instrueren van gebruikers voor het juiste gebruik van de applicatie;
Samenwerken met andere Data Stewards binnen de politie.

Waar ga je werken?
Je gaat werken voor het Datateam van PVR. Dit programma valt onder het productiehuis Handhaving van de Dienst IV. Je gaat werken vanuit het kantoor in Utrecht (HUB50) of vanuit huis. Binnen PVR ontwikkelen multidisciplinaire DevOps-teams snel en flexibel nieuwe functionaliteiten voor de operationele politiediensten. PVR maakt daarvoor gebruik van zogenaamde ‘Agile release trains’.
Het Datateam bestaat twee jaar en gaat uitbreiden van zes naar twaalf mensen. Er werken gedreven en enthousiaste collega’s met verschillende expertises. We staan voor elkaar klaar en steunen ieders behoefte om te groeien. Het Datateam is onderdeel van de Service- en Beheertrein. Dit is de ondersteunende Agile release train voor beheer, services, data en infrastructuur. We werken hybride en onze kantoordagen zijn maandag en woensdag.
Wij geloven dat je het beste tot je recht komt in een omgeving waarin je je prettig voelt. Daarom hechten wij aan een open en informele werksfeer. We moedigen je aan om jezelf te ontwikkelen, ook buiten de grenzen van je vakgebied.
Met bijna 300 andere collega’s binnen het Programma Vernieuwend Registreren werk je in één van de grootste overheid ICT-programma’s van Europa. Een programma dat zowel nationale als internationale aandacht vergaart.
Wil je meer weten over het werken bij het Productiehuis? Bekijk dan deze video!
Wie ben jij?
Als data steward heb je:
hbo (bachelor) bachelor werk- en denkniveau*;
minimaal drie jaar ervaring in data governance of datamanagement;
kennis van frameworks als DAMA-DMBOK;
sterke communicatieve vaardigheden en een proactieve houding;
sterke analytische kwaliteiten en aandacht voor detail en integriteit;
ervaring met SQL en dashboarding;
bij voorkeur kennis van werken in een Agile-omgeving met ontwikkelteams;
bij voorkeur kennis van de politie en de Wet politiegegevens.

Wat wij bieden
De formele standplaats is Utrecht. Er wordt hybride gewerkt, op maandag en woensdag zijn onze kantoordagen. Er is ruimte voor 1 fte. Het betreft een functie voor 32/36 uur per week.
Omdat goede mensen belangrijk zijn binnen de politie investeren we in jouw toekomst. We bieden uitgebreide ontwikkelingsmogelijkheden en een aanstelling in tijdelijke dienst voor een proeftijd van een jaar. Bij voldoende functioneren wordt de aanstelling na een jaar omgezet in een vaste aanstelling. Verder kun je het volgende van ons verwachten:
een bruto maandsalaris van minimaal € 3.734,- en maximaal € 5.882,- (schaal 10 Bbp) op basis van een 36-urige werkweek;
een Individueel Keuzebudget (IKB) dat uit twee delen bestaat:Een bruto deel van 17,86% van je salaris. Met dit budget kun je een deel van je arbeidsvoorwaarden zelf samenstellen. Denk bijvoorbeeld aan het uitbetalen van je budget, het kopen van vakantie-uren of ontwikkelactiviteiten zoals een opleiding.
Een netto deel van € 515,91 ​per jaar. Dit budget kun je bijvoorbeeld gebruiken voor duurzaamheidsdoelen, vakbondscontributie en voor vitaliteit.

een uitstekende pensioenopbouw bij ABP en betaald ouderschapsverlof (meer info over verlof, regelingen en mogelijkheden).

De formele functie binnen het functiegebouw van de politie is bedrijfsvoeringspecialist B, werkterrein informatie- en communicatietechnologie.
Interesse?
Bel of mail met Pieter Ronteltap, product owner Datateam (06 - 28 45 43 66, [e-mail]), als je meer informatie over de functie wilt hebben. Voor vragen over de sollicitatieprocedure bel of mail je Matthijs Reinhard, IT-recruiter (06 - 39 01 43 75, [e-mail]).
Solliciteer uiterlijk 28 september via de sollicitatiebutton.
Acquisitie naar aanleiding van deze vacature wordt niet op prijs gesteld.
Wat verder belangrijk is
Een veiligheidsonderzoek maakt deel uit van de selectieprocedure.
De politie zet in op vernieuwing en cultuurverschillen binnen teams. Divers samengestelde teams presteren beter. Daarom werken we hard aan een open en veilige cultuur waarin divers talent tot bloei komt.

* Je hebt een diploma op hbo (bachelor)-niveau of je bent daaraan gelijkgesteld via EVC. Of je hebt minimaal twee jaar werkervaring op het gevraagde niveau. Dit toon je aan met een erkende functieomschrijving of een formeel vastgestelde vacaturetekst of een ander formeel bewijsstuk. Het bewijsstuk heeft aantoonbaar betrekking op een functie die je daadwerkelijk hebt uitgevoerd en moet herleidbaar zijn tot jouw persoon. Denk aan een werkgeversverklaring waarin het werk- en denkniveau staat opgenomen of een uittreksel uit het HR-systeem waarop je functie en het dienstverband zichtbaar zijn.

Job Description
Within Fugro's flagship initiative VirGeo, we are building and delivering a geodata customer engagement platform. VirGeo is a cloud-hosted ecosystem that lets stakeholders interact with complex geodata, monitor project progress and make informed decisions in near real-time on survey operations. You'll work in a multidisciplinary team that brings Product, Design and DevOps/Engineering together, so the people who shape what we build, how it looks and feels, and how it runs in production all sit around the same table.
AI-enabled engineering is simply how we work. Our developers build alongside AI coding agents every day, we've invested in the instructions, skills and integrations that make those agents effective in our codebase, and we keep finding new ground. That practice only stays ahead if people keep pushing it forward, and that is a large part of this role: as a Senior Full-stack Developer you'll be hands-on across the stack and one of the people who champions the AI mindset within the team. Developing it together with your colleagues, not for them.

Your role

You design and build full-stack web applications and platform services (React, TypeScript, Node.js, Python), with AI agents as a standard part of your toolchain;
You build interactive map-based tools with real-time data integration, layer control and spatial editing, combining open-source, proprietary and partner GIS components;
You build and evolve the cloud-native services that hold up at scale: multi-tenant, resilient and cost-aware, handling large geodata volumes and concurrent users without the experience degrading;
You contribute to architectural decisions, work closely with Product and Design from discovery onwards and with DevOps colleagues on how what you build actually runs, and mentor other developers;
You keep our review practice ahead of our throughput. You are accountable for everything that lands, and you'll help evolve the review habits, tests and guardrails that make high-velocity delivery safe;
You keep advancing our AI-assisted delivery practice alongside the team: decompose work into agent-sized tasks, sharpen the context and instructions that make agents effective in our codebase, and keep human judgement where it matters — architecture, trade-offs, security and code quality;
You extend the shared scaffolding that makes agentic work repeatable: agent instructions, reusable skills and prompts, MCP integrations with our internal systems, automated checks and evaluation of what is actually working;
You champion the AI mindset day to day: pair with colleagues, share what you've learned, challenge habits that no longer hold, and help the whole team get better.

Your track record

You have a minimum of 8 years in full-stack development, ideally in enterprise or data-intensive environments;
You possess deep full-stack craft: strong front-end skills (JavaScript/TypeScript, React or similar) and back-end experience with Python, Java or Node.js, including API design, data modelling and service decomposition. You can reason about a whole system, not only the feature in front of you;
You have solid experience in cloud platforms (AWS, Azure) and containerisation (Docker, Kubernetes), with real experience of what it takes to keep a service healthy in production;
You are experienced with AI coding agents in production work (e.g. Claude Code, Cursor, GitHub Copilot), with a method behind it: context engineering, task decomposition and verifying agent output. You can talk concretely about where agents accelerate you and where they mislead you;
You have a track record of raising the level around you: you share practice, teach by pairing, and are comfortable being challenged by colleagues who are strong in this area too;
Ideally, you are also experienced with mapping libraries, spatial data handling and modern identity & access management. Or the appetite to get deep into marine, offshore and remote sensing data if you haven't worked with it before;
You possess a strong testing discipline and healthy scepticism: the quality bar matters more, not less, when code is generated quickly;
You are familiar with Git, CI/CD and agile ways of working;
You have excellent communication skills and the ability to thrive in a multidisciplinary team, engaging with Product, Design and DevOps as equals rather than handing work over the wall.

What Fugro Offers

A diverse and inclusive working environment;
Based on your relevant experience, the salary ranges from €6100 to €7700. This amount is part of our salary range, with opportunities for growth within the role;
29 holidays per year based on a fulltime employment (of which 4 are appointed by Fugro management) and the possibility to purchase 12 additional days;
The opportunity to work from home in accordance with your manager and corporate policies;
The possibility of setting up an ergonomic home office, including requesting equipment such as hardware or basic office furniture;
Work-from-home allowance of EUR 2,35 net per day, where applicable;
Commuting allowance, with mileage reimbursement for car travel (10-30 km one-way) and an additional EUR 0,10 per km for employees who walk or cycle to work;
Modern pension scheme;
Discounts on supplementary health insurance packages through Fugro’s partner providers;
Free parking in our on-site parking garage, with ample parking facilities and electric vehicle charging stations available;
A bicycle leasing scheme with a company contribution;
Possibility to register with our corporate fitness plan and access to the gym at Fugro’s headquarters, including participation in group fitness classes;
Coaching and support through our EAP (Employee Assistance Program).

Are you interested?

Want to build something truly impactful, in a data-rich professional domain, in a multidisciplinary team that is already working this way and intends to stay ahead? Apply today.

Please visit our Company Page to find out more about what it is like to work at Fugro. If you have any further questions, please contact Umit Nesar, Talent Acquisition Partner, tel. [telefoon]

After you have applied

You will receive an automated confirmation email confirming receipt of your application;
Our Talent Acquisition team (TA) will carefully review your application. If your profile matches the requirements of the role, we will contact you to discuss the next steps;
Depending on the position, the selection process may include one or more interviews and/or assessments;
Throughout the process, we will keep you informed about the progress;
If, at the end of the process, there is a mutual interest from both sides, our TA team will guide you through the offer and onboarding process.
We look forward to welcoming you to Fugro!

